note verify-data.om: fail-closed validation of every published data file and the source inputs
note the generator reads (rules B1-B4 plus the oracle.rs verify_data gates). Callable before any
note output is written: sv_vinit, then sv_vdata kind path (kinds below); it returns true when
note the file passes and reports every failure as `verify: FAIL <RULE> <path>: ...`.
note Ports, with their Rust sources at baseline 3d36bd7 + the RustOracle lane (oracle.rs):
note   machines   components/machines.rs parse(): serde deny_unknown_fields, check_text,
note              check_link, positive ceilings, speed <= its ceiling, on_main/branch, unique ids
note   omega      components/omega.rs parse()+validate(), expand() short links
note   cuda       components/cudaplusplus.rs parse()+validate()+check_status(), pinned expand()
note   research   components/research_status.rs parse()+validate()
note   facts      facts.rs Facts::load (serde shape; unknown fields allowed, known ones once)
note   agents     components/agents.rs Repos::load
note   progress   collector.rs validate_snapshot
note   status     oracle.rs check_status
note   index      oracle.rs check_data_index (exact DATA_FILES set, www url each)
note   pages      oracle.rs check_pages_json (exact PAGES set, each once, title/description,
note              english == path)
note   now        now.json parses
note   quotes     data/quotes.json shape (ids unique) for the voice exemption
note   ledger     ledger_public.rs check_public (project(x) == x)
note Numbers stay lexical (json.om). Where serde would round through f64 this port accepts only
note the exact cases and refuses the rest (documented per check): stricter, never looser.
note Serde strings are any JSON string; sj_load already decoded escapes, so dash checks run on the
note raw file bytes (Rust RAW.contains) AND on decoded strings (a \u2014 escape cannot slip by).
